**frame.hpp defines `input_frame`, the ordered timestamped input unit for the gamepad pipeline.**

## Interface

`input_frame` aggregates `device_id device`, `controller::family family`, `connection link`, `uint64_t sequence`, `latency_span timing`, and `canonical_sample state`, with defaults `family::unknown`, `connection::unknown`, and zero-initialized values.

`operator<< (ostream&, const input_frame&)` serializes frames.

## Contracts

`sequence` increases monotonically per device for ordering and drop detection; `timing.acquired` is producer-stamped, `timing.consumed` consumer-stamped, and `latency()` is meaningful only after consumption.

`types.hpp`, `utility.hpp`, `clock.hpp`, `sample.hpp`, `id.hpp`, and `identity.hpp` supply the field and stream types.